        "original_id": "83d6ac65-7532-5053-abab-ad3358cda21b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Anthony D. \"Tony\" Saletan\n- Roles: folk singer, educator\n- Products: \"Kum ba yah\"\n- Topics: folk music rediscovery, folk revival\n\nFacts:\n- Anthony D. \"Tony\" Saletan is an American folk singer and educator.\n- Anthony D. \"Tony\" Saletan is credited with the modern rediscovery of two well-known folk songs.\n- \"Kum ba yah\" was first recorded in the 1920s.\n- \"Kum ba yah\" became a standard campfire song in Scouting and summer camps.\n- \"Kum ba yah\" gained broader popularity during the folk revival of the 1950s and 1960s.",
