        "original_id": "5f02a07c-5199-5813-8611-4ffd8f30ed73",
        "text": "Anthony D. \"Tony\" Saletan is an American folk singer and educator, who is responsible for the modern rediscovery of two of the genre's best-known songs, one being Kum ba yah, first recorded in the 1920s, and it became a standard campfire song in Scouting and summer camps and enjoyed broader popularity during the folk revival of the 1950s and 1960s.",
